{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":66382863,"ns":0,"title":"Free choice inference","extract":"Free choice is a phenomenon in natural language where a linguistic disjunction appears to receive a logical conjunctive interpretation when it interacts with a modal operator. For example, the following English sentences can be interpreted to mean that the addressee can watch a movie and that they can also play video games, depending on their preference:\n\nYou can watch a movie or play video games.","description":"Phenomenon in natural language","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}